A||||9||sid1200||stereo/speakers||||1||
Z||000000||sid1200||03-24-2000||03:40 AM||||Just put in a 99 Pontiac CD player with the EQ into my 88GT, very easy, looks stock and has red lighting.. now of course with better sound my speakers are sounding like shit, even with 27 k on the car... So I am thinking of putting new speakers in.<P>any advice. how do the front grills come of? and is just a plug and play deal after that.. what about the rears.. i think its a major paing, seat belt and everything... let me know how to proceed.. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||03-24-2000||06:22 AM||||The front grills just pop out / straight up...The rear grills come off with the entire side panel. One screw in front / a couple of clips / the upper seat belt mount. Have fun !!!||||reg||6
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||03-24-2000||08:08 AM||||Where did you get it? Was it as easy as getting the adaptor harness for it? Can you post picts of the CD player?<P>Taking the rears out of the Fiero is not as bad as you think. It is quite easy.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||03-24-2000||08:23 AM||||Nice work, sid.  The front speakers are easy as pie - just take a slim screwdriver and gently pry the speaker covers off one corner at a time.  I've never replaced rear speakers.<P>One question - I heard the newer GM stereos have some kind of Theftlock feature that you have to disable before you can use them in older cars like ours.  Is that true?  And if so, how did you disable it?||||reg||5
Z||000004||terryk||03-24-2000||11:38 AM||||Unless you steal the stereo yourself, the wrecker should have cleared it for you. The procedure is in many of the shop manuals.||||reg||10
Z||000005||Tom88gt||03-24-2000||01:03 PM||||More info on the CD player please.  Does it fill the entire opening or is it DIN size?  Does it stick out?  My JVC sticks out about 1 inch.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||03-24-2000||01:54 PM||||When installing the speakers... You can get an adapter harness ($5-$6 per pair) that will let you plug aftermarket speakers to the Fiero harness. Most sound install places should have them (pretty standard GM stuff). I got mine at Best Buy. <P>On my front speakers the basket was slightly bigger than factory and I had to trim the hole in the dash slightly with a knife to get them to sit in right. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||03-24-2000||06:35 PM||||Tom88gt--Your stereo will sit flush if you cut off the metal mounting tab at the back of the stereo.  (On the car, not the stereo.)  You may need to find another way to keep the back of the stereo from bouncing, though.  I plan on putting my stereo where the dome lights are so this won't be a problem for me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sid1200||03-25-2000||05:58 AM||||Hi all, the stereo mounts flush and is the standard 1.5 din size for the Fiero.. looks perfect although the clock/display is mounted on the left side and is partially blocked by the steering wheel, also the display in in red vs the fiero green, which I though was wierd with the red lighting anyways.  like I said install was easy as pie using the Gm harness adapter, I had to drill slightly different holes for the mounting brackets since the new GM stereos have mounting brakcets built in unlike the old ones which have removable brackets. Still this is no big deal as you just drill small holes over where the old holes where.. Otherwise very ..very easy..<P>I paid 215 for a brand new  99 stereo with harness and shipping (CD with eq, top of the line)  <BR>the guy I got it from has one more I think..email him if you like..<BR>AMAPro661@aol.com||||reg||1
Z||000009||TheFiero64||03-25-2000||09:00 AM||||I added the pontiac radio also. Here is the url I bought it from. <A HREF="http://www.aatechnologies.com/pmyradios/pontiac/16205302.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aatechnologies.com/pmyradios/pontiac/16205302.asp</A>  I love it. It looks stock. Here is the pick of it in the car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CDrad.JPG">  It lights up the factory color. You will need the $20 adapter from Pontiac because the wire harness changed in 1990 or so. the adapter part # is 16140051 It plugs right in.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
